# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. Never commit these.
#
# Private keys (`*.key`, `*.cramkey`, `*.pem`, …) must never enter the working
# tree. `.cramkey` files are archive-signing keys. A private key belongs OUTSIDE
# the tree entirely; the rules below are a backstop, not the primary control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.key
*.cramkey
vendor.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
id_rsa*

# Local env / deploy secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example

# Node dependencies (125 MB, restore with `npm ci`).
node_modules/

# Rust build artifacts (35 GB).
/target
**/target/

# Editor / backup files
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local scratch / test output
/bench/out/
*.log

# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed: this workspace ships binaries, so a locked,
# reproducible dependency set is a feature, not noise.

# Built add-on package, regenerate by zipping firefox-addon/ (identical contents).
cram-addon.zip
